A||N||0||Heisenhund||Mysterious cooling problem - SOLVED!!! (long)||||10||
Z||000000||Heisenhund||05-16-2001||09:32 PM||||Hello all,<P>When I discovered this Forum, I was trying to figure out the source of my cooling problems. The symptoms were: Fast temperature rise into the red with a drop to normal, then a swing back & forth between normal & red, eventually settling down to around normal with occasional rises while driving, especially if the driving were a little "spirited". Many people came forth with many suggestions...with air bubble & bad water pump leading the pack. I replaced the water pump & used about 5 different methods to burp the system. No help. While I was still troubleshooting, the problem manifested itself in a big way. It warped one of the heads & blew the gasket. Since I'd read so much about pulling the cradle & the fact that I wanted to see just exactly what the extent of the damage was, I pulled the engine & took it down to the short block. Along the way I replaced the main & rod bearings (water contamination) the crank (scored when the water displaced all the oil), the timing set (water contamination) and of course got the heads flattened out. When I put everything back together and back in the car, I was looking forward to driving without any troubles. Not so. The temperature problem began immediately. The search was on for the problem only this time I knew what would happen if I didn't find the problem soon enough.<P>I replaced the radiator due to a leak discovered during a pressure test. On the advice of some wise folks here I also replaced the heater core. I replaced all the cooling and heater hoses. Big improvement! Now the temperature would only make one trip up to the red. Sometimes it wouldn't even make it to the red zone, just short of it. But I got to thinking that it may be in the warmup loop when only the heater is in the circuit. I decided to take a look at the water pump again. It's an 86 GT so the heater return goes into a pipe on the pump. When I looked I noticed that the pipe went right into the same suction as the main cooling passage. I thought that might be blocked. I bought a reman pump from AutoZone & put it in. On this pump the heater return goes right to the impeller.<P>Problem solved!!!!<P>Thanks for everyone's help.<P>Heis<BR>||||reg||10
